   "conclusion": {
    "diagnosis": "CNC-01 experienced a transient vibration alarm during ticks 521-524 (7.01-7.37 mm/s, above the 4.50 mm/s threshold) that cleared by tick 525. From tick 525 through the present (tick 545) vibration is normal (~2.2 mm/s, then near-zero as the machine idled), and there is no active alarm on CNC-01. Load was steady (~63-69%) during the event (E8), so it was not a load-driven excursion, and the post-event readings (E7) rule out a developing mechanical fault causing a sustained problem. The root cause of the brief spike is not confirmed - possible chip/debris ingress given the prior way-cover history (E4) or a sensor glitch (H2) - but no current failure requiring repair is indicated. Q6 and Q9 remain open (no independent sensor cross-check or physical inspection since the event), but neither would change the present state: the alarm has cleared and the machine is running normally.",
